          "id": "0644932666e0018ecc2c79479a89787a23cf4214",
          "message": "Enforce flake8-bugbear and RUF013, and state the lint scope once (#616)\n\n* TOOL-1: enforce flake8-bugbear and RUF013, and state the lint scope once\n\nThe register's findings were surfaced by ad-hoc `ruff check --select` runs and\ncaught by nothing. `[tool.ruff.lint] select` now names ruff's defaults - which\nnaming a select would otherwise replace - plus `B` and `RUF013`.\n\nTwo families are ignored with their reason at the ignore: `B023` (24 sites) and\n`B905` (22), both needing per-site judgement. The six findings in the rest of\n`B` are fixed rather than ignored: two `warnings.warn` calls gained\n`stacklevel=2`, and four bare-name expressions - two probing for an injected\n`profile`, two asserting an attribute access raises - carry a `noqa` naming the\nintent.\n\nWhat `prototypes/` is exempt from moves off the pre-commit hook into\n`[tool.ruff.lint] exclude`, so a bare `uv run ruff check` and the hook cannot\ndisagree. That exclusion needs a glob: a bare `\"prototypes\"` is accepted there\nand matches nothing, unlike the top-level `exclude`.\n\n`tests/test_lint_configuration.py` covers the two silent failures - a `select`\nthat dropped a default, and an exemption that exempts nothing - each verified to\nfail on the mutation it names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* TOOL-1: rewrite the item to hold only its remainder\n\nThe rule set it asked for is enabled, so what is left is the two ignored\nfamilies - 46 sites needing individual judgement - and the ruff 0.16 bump they\ngate, which is one item because clearing `B023` removes a quarter of that wall.\n\nThe 2026-08-14 reading that `B023`, `B905`, `A001`, `A002` and `PLW2901` were\nclean repo-wide is re-measured on 0.15.22 and stale for all five: the entry said\nthey \"could be enabled on their own\", which would have cost a pass to discover\notherwise.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* TOOL-1: file the changelog as a fragment, correct the counts, close the test gaps\n\nReview findings, all six confirmed.\n\nThe changelog bullet was written straight into the unreleased section of\nCHANGELOG.rst, which the changelog policy forbids in bold: fragments exist so\nthat concurrent branches do not all own the same lines, and five other\nworktrees are active against this tree. It moves to\nchangelog.d/internal/ruff-bugbear-enforced.rst and is cut to a few sentences.\n\n`B905` is 27 sites across 18 files, not 22. The wrong figure was in the ignore\ncomment, in the item and in the ranking row's arithmetic.\n\nThe item claimed the enabled rule set covered \"the register's ad-hoc findings\",\nwhich is false for `A001`, `A002`, `PLW2901` and `PLR09xx` - 24 sites in\nfamilies that `B` and `RUF013` do not contain, which the rewrite would have\ndropped from the register entirely. It now carries all six unenforced families\nin a measured table, 75 sites, and says the counts are not regenerated by\nanything.\n\nTwo tests asserted less than their own docstrings claimed:\n\n  - the default-rules test read `select` out of the TOML, so it stayed green\n    while `ignore`, `per-file-ignores` or a shadowing selector switched the same\n    coverage off. It now lints a snippet per rule and asserts the rule fires;\n    both routes verified to turn it red. `E9` is dropped with the reason - ruff\n    reports a syntax error whatever is selected, so there is nothing to probe.\n  - the hook test rested on `--force-exclude` without asserting it. A hook\n    passing `--no-force-exclude` would lint `prototypes/` from `make hook` alone\n    while every other assertion here stayed green; that is now asserted, and\n    verified to turn red.\n\n`_ruff` also raises on a ruff that failed to run, rather than returning empty\noutput that every assertion would read as \"no findings\" - reachable from a\n`test`-only environment, since ruff is in the `dev` group.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
